// F6 — struct move-then-read ownership fixture.
//
// `let q = p` moves the struct value out of `p`. The subsequent projected
// field read `print(p.x)` is a B0005 use-after-move under the current
// ownership/book semantics.
//
// This fixture is retained in the fallback CLI matrix as regression coverage
// for the stale expectation that VM mode succeeds or that JIT emits a fallback
// line. Both modes should fail before execution with B0005.
type P { x: int, name: string }
let p = P { x: 1, name: "a" }
let q = p
print(p.x)
